B:Edward Holmes MS, c1846, Beverley, Yorkshire.
N:The regiment was formed in 1689 by David Leslie, 3rd Earl of Leven & was known as
N:Leven's Regiment, becoming Semphill's Regiment of Foot under which name it fought
N:at the battle of Culloden. In 1751 it became the 25th Foot and was the county regiment
N:of Sussex from 1782 - 1805. Its recruiting area then moved to the Scottish Borders
N:and it was called the King's Own Borderers, becoming the King's Own Scottish
N:Borderers in 1887.
