N:From "A Supplementary List of Operas" by W.L.Hubbard, 1910. :-
N:"Gustavus III, or The Masked Ball Grand opera in five acts. Music by Auber, text by Scribe,
K:C
N:first produced at Paris in 1833. Soon after in England. The story is historical; place,
N: Stockholm; time, 1792. Verdi's " Masked Ball " appeared twenty-six years later withplace
N:and characters changed. Auber's opera was so popular that it literally took Europe off its
N: feet, and the famous Gustavus gallop has been danced all over the world."
