Q:1/4=80
B:Edward Holmes MS, c1846, Beverley, Yorkshire.
N:"Ew-Bughts" or "Ewe-boughts" are small inclosures, or pens, into which the farmers drive
N:their milch ewes, morning and evening, in order to milk them. They are commonly made
N:with fale-dykes, i.e. earthen dykes. (From the Glossary to "Reliques of Ancient English
N:Poetry: consisting of Old Heroic Ballads, Songs and other pieces etc." 1823)
N:Key signature??
N:NB1 = Ad'o So'o. Perhaps means  "Adagio Sostenuto". = Slow & Sustained. (Italian)
N:NB2 = Un-matched repeat.??
